A||||3||Jhonny||EGR tube and PVC hose on the run ...||||4||
Z||000000||Jhonny||12-14-2000||07:03 AM||||<BR>I removed the upper plenum to gain access to the EGR tube and of course it was broken.<BR>Then I noticed that a P.O had closed the hole to the plenum with a gasket and letting<BR>the end of tube hang freely under the plenum.<BR>Could this damage the engine in someway ?<P>At the same time I also noticed that the PCV hose going from the front rocker cover to the air filter assembly also was loose.<BR>What's your thoughts about this folks?<P>/// Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR><A HREF="http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html" TARGET=_blank> Welcome to Vadstena</A>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Raydar||12-14-2000||09:49 AM||||Jhonny,<P>The gasket should have a <I>small</I> hole in it. About the size of a pencil eraser, if I remember correctly. It shouldn't be as large as the EGR tube. <BR>If the tube is broken, it shouldn't hurt the engine. The main symptom that you would notice is that it will idle faster than normal. <BR>There are varying opinions regarding whether the EGR being blocked will hurt the engine. I believe that it can, after many miles. Others say that it won't hurt anything.<P>The PCV pipe will be a bit loose, where it fits into the valve cover. There shouldn't be any air leaks, though. That would not be good.<P>Welcome to the Forum!<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jhonny||12-15-2000||02:05 AM||||<BR>How important is size of the hole in the  gasket ?   <BR>I believe the gasket hole at the EGR side<BR>are of the same as the tube diameter.<P>/// Jhonny<P><P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR><A HREF="http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html" TARGET=_blank> Welcome to Vadstena</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-15-2000||02:22 PM||||The gasket closest to the EGR valve will have a large hole. Same size as the tube. The gasket at the plenum end will have the small hole. I believe that GM designed it that way to limit the amount of exhaust that gets recycled.||||reg||1
